    "semantics": "§4a intent law (re-recorded 2026-11-13; every pre-§4a pin below is a documented legacy-defect change, not silent drift): an artifact WORD is not an artifact REQUEST. Quoted/code spans are masked first; clauses split on [.!?\\n;]+ AFTER alnum-dot-alnum runs ('file.docx', 'v2.5') become spaces (filename/version/decimal dots are not clause boundaries — 'create file.docx' binds docs); an artifact word counts as requested only when a production cue precedes it in the same clause — all cue/artifact/direction/negation/meta relations compare MATCH STARTS by order only, never end-vs-start (adjacent matches share their boundary character, so end-vs-start is off-by-one there; fixed in both engines 2026-11-13; this is why 'export as xlsx'/'generate pdf report' were misses before) (cue vocabulary is ENGLISH-ONLY — a non-Latin verb with a Latin artifact word falls gracefully to standard_chat); negation before the word vetoes it; convert/export governs the word directly as the SOURCE format (the word after a to/into/as direction word is the output); summary/outline-style meta phrases mark discussed material; two+ requested intents are ambiguous ('in-process-deliverable-ambiguous') — INTENT_ORDER precedence retired. Unicode \\p{L}/\\p{N}/\\p{M} consuming word classes in BOTHengines: caféexcel/résumébuilder no longer split, bare résumé matches its own word, résumé2 honestly misses. Honest confidence: 0.8 verb-bound, 0.5 miss/ambiguous — the retired blanket 1.0 was false certainty. Anatomy/3d/cad vocabulary stays standard_chat (retired 2026-11-06/07) unless a §4a cue-bound request survives ('make an exploded diagram in html' -> html_render; 'interior design with html' -> html_render because 'design' is a production cue now).",
    "comparison": "semantic",
    "notes": "Field-for-field (mode/skill/decided_by/trim/confidence) — regex existence only, no span capture. Re-recorded 2026-11-13 for the §4a intent law (brief §4): the OLD corpus pinned the ASCII-\\b quirks, INTENT_ORDER precedence and confidence 1 as contracts; brief §6 reclassifies those as legacy defects, so their pins moved to the OPPOSITE behavior.",
